# Checking the project

Two commands answer questions about the project you are in: `howdy check`
says whether it is in good shape, and `howdy routes` says what it serves.

## howdy check

```sh
howdy check
```

`howdy check` checks the project the way to check any change to it:

- *format*: `gleam format --check`, over `src`, `test` and `dev`;
- *build*: `gleam build`, reporting the compiler's warnings;
- *test*: `gleam test`.

Every check runs, except the tests when the build fails. The output of a
check that fails is shown, and the command exits with status 1 if any did:

```
🤠 howdy check

  ✓ format  gleam format --check src test dev
  ✓ build   gleam build
  ✓ test    gleam test
```

Pass `--fix` to format the sources first, rather than report them:

```sh
howdy check --fix
```

`howdy check --json` prints one object with each check's outcome, for a
script or a coding agent, with the output of a check that failed:

```json
{
  "ok": true,
  "checks": [
    {"name": "format", "status": "passed", "command": "gleam format --check src test dev"},
    {"name": "build", "status": "passed", "command": "gleam build"},
    {"name": "test", "status": "passed", "command": "gleam test"}
  ]
}
```

A project made by `howdy new` tells coding agents, in `AGENTS.md`, to run
`howdy check` after every change and fix what it reports before moving on.
The tests need the database: on PostgreSQL, start it with
`docker compose up -d` first.

## howdy routes

```sh
howdy routes
```

`howdy routes` lists every route the project serves: its method and path,
the controller that declares it, and the file and line it is on, so a
route can be found from its path:

```
METHOD  PATH            CONTROLLER          DEFINED AT
GET     /up             howdy.health_check  src/my_app.gleam:47
GET     /api/todos      todos.controller    src/my_app/features/todos/todo_controller.gleam:21
GET     /api/todos/:id  todos.controller    src/my_app/features/todos/todo_controller.gleam:24
POST    /api/todos      todos.controller    src/my_app/features/todos/todo_controller.gleam:28
GET     /               home.controller     src/my_app/features/home/home_controller.gleam:13
*       /               static.serve        src/my_app.gleam:42
```

Routes are read from the sources, without building the app: the
controllers registered in `app()` in `src/<project>.gleam`, in the order
they are registered, and the routes each one declares with
`controller.get`, `post`, `put`, `patch`, `delete` or `route`, and the
endpoint functions of Howdy OpenAPI. A controller that comes from a
package, such as auth's pages or the static files, is a mount, with method
`*`, at the path it is given. Routes from `dev/`, such as the admin at
`/_howdy`, are served only by `gleam dev`. A
[health check](/docs/guides/health-checks) mounted with
`howdy.health_check` comes first, at `/up` or the path `health.at` gives
it, because it is answered before any route.

A route built some other way, such as in a loop or a helper, is not seen.

`howdy routes --json` prints the routes as an array, with whether each is
guarded:

```json
[
  {
    "method": "GET",
    "path": "/api/todos",
    "file": "src/my_app/features/todos/todo_controller.gleam",
    "line": 21,
    "controller": "todos.controller",
    "guarded": false
  }
]
```
